{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>There is no good.</b> He found no good in all this toil of his labor, except food and drink. And רק is lacking [i.e., should be supplied], or its equivalent. Likewise it is: <b>there is no good in a man</b> — <b>except that he eat and drink</b>, and like it: <b>for they do not know how to do evil</b>. And the matter of <b>for it is from the hand of Elohim</b> is that the one who gathers wealth is like a guardian, and he has no authority to touch it until Elohim gives him authority."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:16.052070610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}